# Landlord Timeline — property-team outcomes only

Timeline (right rails, Overview feed, operations history) is for the **property team**. Show what happened in the real world — not workflow-engine receipts.

## Show

Work opened, vendor accepted/declined, visit window, response time exceeded, resident text that changed the job, rent reminder sent, payment received, lease notice sent, escalation that needs a decision.

## Hide

| Kind | Examples |
|---|---|
| Pipeline stages | `workflow.trigger` / `classify` / `route` / `act` / `log` → “Workflow started”, “Classified”, “Routed”, “Action taken”, “Logged” |
| SMS transport | `sms.delivered`, `sms.message_received` (outcomes live on domain events) |

Keep `workflow.escalate` — that is a landlord-facing “needs attention” outcome.

Rail Timeline must stay a **complete operational story** (reported → classified as issue → dispatched when relevant → response delayed). Hiding plumbing must not collapse 3 beats into 1 leftover engine row. Prefer the ticket story; only append extra domain facts (vendor declined, photos added).

Copy stays plain language (no “workflow”, event types, IDs). Prefer `metadata.message` when it is already landlord-facing.

## Where it lives

- Shared filter: `isHiddenPipelineTimelineEventType` / `isVisibleLandlordTimelineDescription` in `src/lib/landlordFacingTimeline.ts`
- Rails: `isVisibleSlaTimelineEntry` / `timelineFromWorkflowEvents`
- Feed: `isLandlordFacingFeedEvent` in `propertyOperationsGraph.ts`

## Do not

- Dump `workflow_events` onto Timeline without the landlord-facing filter
- Replace the operational story with leftover `workflow.act` / `workflow.log` / `workflow.trigger` rows
- Add new pipeline-stage labels to Timeline to “explain the engine”
- Treat SMS delivery receipts as Timeline rows
